<http://data.silknow.org/production/018473df-78e3-32b7-8814-304e41a6575d>
        a                       ecrm:E12_Production ;
        ecrm:P108_has_produced  <http://data.silknow.org/object/bb1838be-3c46-3a33-90e4-0a32c11d8dc4> ;
        ecrm:P126_employed      "2 shots between pile. Gilt or silver (?) metal wrap, Z-twist, variable tightness.  Uses two different types of kilaptan.  Selvedges: 1cm.  Uses blue silk warps that use more warp threads closer to the edge"@en , "count 16 and 24"@en , "the extreme striations of the green/blue is carried through on the back, which makes it unlikely that the evenness is the result of fading due to light.  One end has tightly wrapped kilaptan."@en , "gold in the larger parts"@en , "pile counts: warps 10, along weft 14.  Brocade structure: wholly brocaded, 4/1 twill"@en , "Voided and brocaded silk velvet. Satin foundation structure: 4/1 satin, unplied ivory silk filament warp, 1 strand ivory cotton weft.  Satin and velvet warp order 3-1. Velvet structure: red and green silk"@en , "though it is difficult to tell, the main motifs use both gold and silver thread"@en , "the silver is in the interior part of the moons at the bottom of each roundel"@en , "at one band, the wefts float over a set of warps. Selvedge twill: 2/1 or 3/1. 1.2 cm. and 1 cm.\n\nBack restored and covered with red cotton cloth"@en ;
        ecrm:P126_employed      <http://data.silknow.org/vocabulary/617> , <http://data.silknow.org/vocabulary/900> ;
        ecrm:P32_used_general_technique
                <http://data.silknow.org/vocabulary/526> ;
